<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolkiah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sultan Bolkiah, Nakhoda Ragam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolkiah was the fifth sultan of Brunei, who reigned from about 1485 to 1524. Remembered in legend as Nakhoda Ragam, the singing captain, he led naval expeditions that extended Brunei's power over much of the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> and into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>. His reign is regarded as Brunei's golden age, and his tomb is at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kota-batu">Kota Batu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolkiah.jpg" alt="Bolkiah" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bubbha at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bolkiah-tomb.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
